# sync.env — install as ${PF_CONFIG_DIR}/sync.env
# (default /etc/private-finances/sync.env), owned by root, mode 600.
#
# Read by one service in compose.yaml: worker, the short-lived container the
# host's systemd timers start for each scheduled job (bank imports, exchange
# rates, reports, the assets snapshot), after app.env. A key set here
# overrides the same key in app.env for those jobs only.
#
# On a container host this file can be empty, and it must exist: compose
# refuses a missing env_file. Everything the imports need is either set by
# compose.yaml (CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY, ENABLEBANKING_SESSION_DIRECTORY) or
# already in app.env, because the dashboard needs it too (the Enable Banking
# application IDs and key paths, MONOBANK_INCLUDE_JARS, ETH_RPC_URL).
# Which imports run at all is decided by marker files under
# /etc/private-finances/schedules, not by settings: see docs/scheduling.md.

# ---- Reports -----------------------------------------------------------------

# Optional, default Europe/Riga. The IANA time zone whose calendar decides when
# a month or week has ended for the scheduled report job. Other screens still
# use Europe/Riga regardless (see "Known gaps" in docs/first-install.md).
#REPORT_TIMEZONE=Europe/Riga

# ---- Manual jobs run through the worker service ------------------------------
# Only for commands an operator runs by hand, for example
# docker compose --profile tools run --rm worker node dist/src/categorize-cli.js

# Optional, default 10000. The most transactions one categorize run may file.
# That job also needs AUTO_CATEGORIZE_CLEAR_EXPENSES=true (set it here for the
# worker) and the OpenAI settings in app.env.
#CATEGORIZE_MAX_TRANSACTIONS=10000
# Optional. The bank a manual `sync-cli.js enablebanking <owner> <from> <to>`
# run imports when the command line names none: wise, revolut, swedbank or lhv.
# The scheduled imports always name the bank and ignore it.
#ENABLEBANKING_BANK=wise
